SUMMARY:Heartland Marimba Festival – FREE
DESCRIPTION:Make the Ware Center part of your Lancaster First Friday route!
  7 p.m. • Lobby How did an instrument with roots in Africa find its way 
 to the classical music stage—and what does Pennsylvania have to do with 
 it? Join members of Heartland Marimba for a fascinating\, hands-on explora
 tion of the marimba’s sounds\, science\, and history. Discover how its d
 istinctive acoustics work\, trace its journey from Africa through Central 
 America\, and learn how U.S. companies and performers helped bring the ins
 trument into classical music. You’ll also uncover some surprising local 
 connections\, including Clair Musser\, the Manheim-born musician widely re
 garded as the “godfather” of classical marimba\, and the Marimba Queen
 s\, an all-female ensemble based in Lancaster that toured the country for 
 nearly 20 years\, beginning in the 1930s. Whether you’re a music lover\,
  history buff\, or simply curious about this remarkable instrument\, there
 ’s something to discover! More First Friday fun: From 5–7 p.m.\, Mille
 rsville students will lead free\, hands-on creative activities for kids in
  the lobby. Admission: FREE and open to the public! Accessibility: A touch
  tour will be available for blind and low-vision patrons. Please contact B
 arry Kornhauser for more information.\n\nPrice: Not supplied by this sourc
 e\; check event details\n\nSchedule listed: Fri\, Nov 06\, 2026 07:00 PM E
